nfty,2) \\cup [-1,3]$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068521 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9cf4daed-1d80-5a74-90dc-b0b1da0ce6b9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068521 #edb/ref 1074 "If we plot these two intervals on number lines, we get the following:\n\n![](images/27/2720cafe76aff8eb85ca65851570087505ee57a4b51904ee075aa86436cfc475.png)\n\n![](images/c3/c379dc0e0c371832a53e62da4505cfc0b03df50efc7241c0100794a191c8fb97.png)\n\nThe union of the two intervals consists of all the points which are contained within at least one of the intervals. So, to graph the union of the two intervals, we take the graphs of the individual intervals and lay them on top of each other.\n\nThe resulting graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/c4/c43257d8d30711804848039b3b8458302e0030e7512fb7cbf1f4b697263e5155.png)\n\nThis graph represents the interval $(-\\infty,3]$. So, the union $(-\\infty,2) \\cup [-1,3]$ simplifies to the interval $(-\\infty,3]$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068631 #edb/ref 1069 "e-6278" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068631 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the union of the intervals shown on the number lines below?\n\n![](images/60/603da954fd0e711ffa4879c51db847095edd9b1f256bbef66ad9de91c8cb31b4.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068631 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "489ef834-7015-5592-a5f5-b0daa3bc9f7b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068631 #edb/ref 1074 "We have the following number lines:\n\n![](images/60/603da954fd0e711ffa4879c51db847095edd9b1f256bbef66ad9de91c8cb31b4.png)\n\nThe union of the two intervals consists of all the points which are contained within at least one of the intervals. So, to graph the union of the two intervals, we take the graphs of the individual intervals and lay them on top of each other.\n\nThe resulting graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/58/5829d80a75446161fba99c08b361083a025a0c341fa41cf0608867d220dfa538.png)\n\nThe graph represents the interval $(-1,\\infty)$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068666 #edb/ref 1069 "e-952" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068666 #edb/ref 1071 "Express the compound inequality $x < 4$ or $x \\ge 10$ using interval notation." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068666 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d0e51ce4-7f83-545e-9c3c-b79bf58d0eab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068666 #edb/ref 1074 "We can represent the compound inequality on a number line, as follows:\n\n![](images/26/26594fb87ed7eca0803d554e4a1fbd3d3719cc01ba4e70f96126b73924ac5769.png)\n\nThis number line consists of the interval $(-\\infty, 4)$ as well as the interval $[10, \\infty)$.\n\nSo, we can express the compound inequality as the union of these two intervals:\n\n$$\n(-\\infty, 4) \\:{\\cup}\\: [10, \\infty)\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068667 #edb/ref 1069 "e-954" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068667 #edb/ref 1071 "Express $\\left(-\\infty, -1 \\right) \\cup [2, \\infty)$ as an inequality." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068667 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c575830c-0100-5cec-a3f8-70e29cba3b54" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068667 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we graph the two intervals on a number line:\n\n![](images/eb/ebc7db3faf2d9eafb887e93e9cf3613853914bf02ef87b6f63b638494c55a2ac.png)\n\nThe interval\n\n$$\n\\left(-\\infty, -1 \\right)\n$$\n\ncan be expressed as the inequality $x < -1$.\n\nLikewise, the interval $[2, \\infty)$ can be expressed as the inequality\n\n$$\nx \\geq 2\n$$\n\nSo, the union of these intervals represents the compound inequality\n\n$$\nx < -1 \\text{or} x \\geq 2\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068787 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069353 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068787 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069354 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068787 #edb/ref 1039 "Expressing a Union of Overlapping Intervals Given Graphically" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068787 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186068631 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068787 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "b6619614-04df-5a22-afa8-77a41b016330" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068811 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049162 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068811 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069028 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068811 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069449 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068811 #edb/ref 1039 "Expressing an Inequality as a Union of Intervals" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068811 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186068666 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068811 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "eee95dd4-7d0c-5c18-bcb0-9b033e0cb509" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068812 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069202 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068812 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069325 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068812 #edb/ref 1039 "Expressing a Union of Non-Overlapping Intervals as an Inequality" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068812 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186068667 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068812 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "1300ab0b-313f-5489-a836-79cf200082f6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068906 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069194 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068906 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069450 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068906 #edb/ref 1039 "Expressing a Union of Overlapping Intervals" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068906 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186068521 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068906 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "5a74d2eb-fe22-5c2d-b31f-9446f8f080d3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068985 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069707 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068985 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069739 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068985 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069740 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068985 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069741 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068985 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069883 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068985 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069884 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068985 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068985 #edb/ref 1045 "Unions of Intervals" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068985 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186069739 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068985 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050229 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068985 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "4207750e-9221-5674-acec-1d120f06d3d3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069354 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186067294 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069354 #edb/ref 1069 "q-44865" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069354 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/e6/e68b6cd55df9e2c81409910829e2194576a5e249a171c34ff28e30e3d34cb807.png)\n\nWhat is the union of the intervals shown on the number lines above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069354 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e818c059-b2ba-57e5-8dad-9805a5c081f6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069450 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186067870 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069450 #edb/ref 1069 "q-59475" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069450 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify the union of intervals $(-2, 3]∪(1, ∞)$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069450 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c4302277-24d7-598f-a06e-35350706f2d5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069707 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069883 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069707 #edb/ref 1061 23592 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069707 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d06f5800-1be7-5609-b455-6c1d38707d7d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069707 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068787 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069739 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069740 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069739 #edb/ref 1061 3167 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069739 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b0fb12dd-e8a8-5a10-9f60-f1d994766e86" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069739 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186069934 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069740 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069741 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069740 #edb/ref 1061 3168 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069740 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "325b8527-c92b-5ecd-b56e-5c14cc0b6cf5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069740 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068811 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069741 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069884 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069741 #edb/ref 1061 3172 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069741 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "655fb4ff-9084-5ff0-9f76-e5c230ef695e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069741 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068812 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069883 #edb/ref 1061 5562 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069883 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5832944b-422f-5154-8451-6dc2929473ea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069883 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068906 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069884 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069707 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069884 #edb/ref 1061 5564 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069884 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "423acfad-41bd-5f38-909c-92b01da8da23" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069884 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186069950 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069934 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose we want to represent the following number line graph using interval notation:\n\n![](images/0b/0bf5e420e2929032c11964e15d710014fb34d559aa065428b9d57fff14d10eb0.png)\n\nThis number line consists of the interval $(-3, -1)$ as well as the interval $(1, 3)$.\n\nTo express the combination of these two intervals, we create a **union of intervals** using the **union sign** $\\cup$ as follows:\n\n$$\n(-3, -1) \\cup (1, 3)\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069934 #edb/ref 1065 1422 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069934 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "3a3780a2-b10d-5640-a797-ea56e4eee1af" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069934 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069950 #edb/ref 1064 "Sometimes, the union of two intervals can simplify into a single interval. For example, consider the union\n\n$$\n(-3,2) \\cup (0,4)\n$$\n\nIf we plot these two intervals on number lines, we get the following:\n\n![](images/4a/4aafe0cdf9f5b27d99538bbaacbf567ded823189399e518f2ead7381da35e84c.png)\n\n![](images/4a/4a26c3aa30f2aab862b31624ba08e3a575fee511e46f89abf62c26aa38dd811f.png)\n\nThe union of the two intervals consists of all the points which are contained within at least one of the intervals. So, to graph the union of the two intervals, we take the graphs of the individual intervals and lay them on top of each other.\n\nThe resulting graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/83/835f7e883cf1aba1945f9cecab382ddc163e1c2413895c8b2f8d1d61ae81d1a0.png)\n\nThis graph represents the interval $(-3,4)$. So, the union $(-3,2) \\cup (0,4)$ simplifies to the interval $(-3,4)$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069950 #edb/ref 1065 1798 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069950 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "a4af4ad6-6c9c-552b-8ab9-8cb92744e7c6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069950 #edb/ref 1067 "The Union of Overlapping Intervals" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
